{
  "analysis": "Inclusion is the failing class (recall 0.20, 148/179 missed): misses are tiny (median 34.7px vs 90.5px train), faint, thin vertical streaks; low-size tertile recall is 0.075 and nearly all misses are low-contrast. Patches (recall 0.61) and scratches (recall 0.54) both lose mainly on the small/low-contrast tertile (0.47 and 0.40 recall), with missed medians 51px and 41.6px. So all three classes need small, low-contrast synthetic examples; inclusion needs the biggest share.",
  "allocation": {"inclusion": 25, "patches": 15, "scratches": 10},
  "params": {
    "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.30, "scale_max": 0.80, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [11, 150, 287, 50, 268, 277]},
    "patches": {"scale_min": 0.40, "scale_max": 0.90, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
    "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.30, "scale_max": 0.70, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
  },
  "rationale": "Inclusion gets 25 images from the faint/thin vertical streak sources (11, 150, 287, 50, 268, 277) scaled to 0.3-0.8x to hit the ~35px missed size band, since the detector almost never sees small low-contrast inclusions. Patches (15) use prefer_small over all blob sources at 0.4-0.9x to produce ~35-75px low-contrast blobs matching the 51px missed median. Scratches (10) use prefer_small at 0.3-0.7x to shorten the long bright lines into the short thin ~40px strokes that are being missed. All classes stay well under the 80-image diminishing-return zone and above the 10-image floor, and same-class backgrounds keep paste texture realistic."
}

